I go to the billing counter.
I have three new clothes in my hand.
A big blue kurta, a white shirt, and a red dupatta.
I put the clothes on the counter.
I say, "Bhaiya, I want these clothes."
The bhaiya smiles.
He says, "Yes madam, I make the bill now."
He makes the bill for the clothes.
I ask, "Bhaiya, what is the total amount?"
The bhaiya says, "Madam, the total is one thousand six hundred rupees."
This price is very good.
I take money out of the bag.
I give the full amount to the bhaiya.
The bhaiya says thank you.
I happily pack the new clothes in my bag.
These cotton clothes are very good for the summer.
Now I feel very good.
I want to wear the new blue kurta to the office.
